From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:16:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 077/148] [ae-patch] Show a native Claude session's live
 progress line in the chat's Working row
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

While Claude Code streams one long tool call (a Write of a 400-line file,
say), it writes nothing to the transcript until the call finishes, so the web
chat showed only a generic "Working" row while the terminal showed a live
spinner such as "Crunching... (4m 42s, 24.5k tokens)". The "last activity"
aside also read "just now" because usage, status and cost posts stamped it.

The forwarder now parses the spinner line from the pane capture it already
takes every two seconds (ae_pane_progress) and posts a transient
external_session_progress event when the line changes, plus one clear when it
goes away. The server validates it (label up to 40 characters, elapsed up to
20, tokens up to 30) and publishes it as a transient session.progress SSE
event; nothing is persisted.

The chat store keeps the latest line per conversation and clears it when an
item or tool row lands, when the session stops running, and on a rebind. The
Working row shows "Crunching · 4m 42s · 24.5k tokens" when no tool step is
known, and "no output yet; a long step may be writing" after a minute with no
content. "Last activity" now counts only content events (text, reasoning,
items, tool output), not usage, status, model, presence or progress events.

Review fixes folded in:
- A line no post refreshed for 30 seconds is dropped from the row, so a
  stalled forwarder or a dropped host never leaves a frozen line.
- The relay posts when the label or token count changes, otherwise at most
  every 10 seconds, and sends elapsed_s; the row ticks the elapsed time
  locally in the terminal's format.
- The pane parse finds the input box with the same opening-rule logic as
  the composer check (now _composer_opening_rule), so a short pane with an
  earlier rule still finds the spinner.
- A failed capture, a pane with no input box, or a visible /btw overlay
  reads as unknown: nothing is posted or cleared.
- A /clear or /fork rotation clears the line it left on the old session,
  and session.superseded clears it in the web.
- The switch to running stamps last activity, so a turn starting after a
  long idle does not read as quiet; the no-output hint dates from the later
  of the last content and the turn start.
- The type string and field bounds live in omnigent/util/ae_session_progress
  and are shared by the forwarder and the route.
